  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through tonight: Rain showers exiting to the east this\nmorning with the surface trough remaining in place will provide a\nsmall chance(10-30%) for fog to sneak back in to the far \nnortheast during the usual hours from 3-10AM. This will probably \nremain patchy and will most likely impact just Plentywood and not\nmove any farther SW into Poplar and Wolf Point. The reason for \nthe small chance comes down to clearing skies in the afternoon \nand early evenings hours which may allow the surface layer to dry \nout further and prevent fog from occuring here. \n\nWednesday afternoon through Sunday night: Above normal\ntemps of 10 to 15 degrees remain across the region though the \nweekend as a ridge plops itself over the front range and sits for \na long period. Conditions should remain dry as well.\n\nMonday onward: Model ensembles break apart here with the GEFS\ndragging the ridge out east and replacing it with a trough, while\nEC grouping remaining in place or washes the ridge out slowly. \nLow confidence from here onward. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNo deviations from NBM. \n\nHigh confidence through Friday night.\nModerate Confidence through Sunday night.\nLow confidence Monday onward\n\nGAH",
